cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OpenReadout in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: OpenReadout
abstract: >-
  One static binary that reads raw lab-instrument files (microscopy, mass spectrometry,
  chromatography, flow cytometry, NMR, electrophysiology, spectroscopy, plate readers, qPCR and
  more), reports what is in them as JSON, exports them to open formats and exposes the same
  operations as MCP tools.
authors:
  - name: "The OpenReadout Authors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/openreadout/openreadout"
url: "https://openreadout.github.io/openreadout/"
# Dual-licensed: CFF reads a list of licenses as alternatives (MIT OR Apache-2.0).
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - microscopy
  - mass spectrometry
  - flow cytometry
  - electrophysiology
  - NMR
  - file formats
  - OME-TIFF
  - OME-Zarr
  - Model Context Protocol
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-02"
